{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1321014-what-are-the-must-haves-for-a-4-hour-mage-demo","id":1321014,"title":"What are the must haves for a 4 hour Mage demo?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-26T12:52:32-07:00","id":1321014,"title":"What are the must haves for a 4 hour Mage demo?","content":"You're a storyteller and you've been asked to come up with a canned adventure to run new players through that have otherwise never played the game. You have four hours including whatever goes into explaining the game. What would you consider the must haves to show off Mage in the most efficient way possible? What assistance would you give players like rote cards or other cheat sheets to get them moving as quickly as possible? Assume characters are pre-generated or largely pre-generated (players can add finishing touches but the concept of the character is largely set).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T13:29:27-07:00","id":1321026,"title":"","content":"If I'm trying to show off Mage, my primary goal is to show off the creativity of the magic system. Which is kinda hard to do for new players.<br /> <br /> What I've done to speed things up and show things off?<br /> <br /> 1) Cheat Sheet of the basics of what each Sphere can do at each level (there was a decent version of this in the 2e Core book that's not hard to update, and now M20 has a decent chart of standard effects), the common modifiers, and a simple breakdown of coincidental vs. vulgar.<br /> <br /> 2) Attach an index card sized cheat sheet to each of the pre-gens with broadly worded single sentences about what the common things they character does with magic. This helps explain the character a bit in relatable terms and is a jumping off board without relying on writing down rotes. Ex: &quot;[Character] can control the flow of any form of common energy using [instrument], but can't create it from nothing.&quot; &quot;[Character] uses their magic to detect flaws via [instrument] letting them both know if something's wrong with an object brought into their pawn shop, and if the sales pitch is hinky.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) Explain how I want them to declare using magic very clearly and not have them worry about the mechanics as much as possible when they do. Basically state things like the card attached is already phrased,either adapting what's on the card or using the #1 sheet to make new ones, then they can make a case for coincidental/vulgar in one sentence, declare WP/qunitessence/taking their time/etc. and make a case for any modifiers in one sentence.<br /> <br /> 4) I then transparently walk through the ST adjudication process so they see how their intent gets translated into the final roll.<br /> <br /> 5) They roll, results occur, game on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}